f 1080 "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}(8-\\sqrt{2})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554372 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554372 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e88ae27f-5535-584b-9730-b1ae58287e87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554373 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{16\\pi }{3}(4-\\sqrt{2})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554373 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554373 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e892a90b-d1ba-521a-b1de-129de62c0978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554511 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c5e8aa5a-ac76-5fe7-8cbb-d1e2111d6174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554602 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554602 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554602 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554602 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=2{e}^{t/2},\\,y={e}^{t},\\,t\\in [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3].\n$$\n\nCalculate the surface area generated when this curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554602 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8fe28743-a486-54a9-8fdd-bcbf858bcbbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554602 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince our curve is given in parametric form, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${t}_{1}=0$ to ${t}_{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.$ \n\nComputing the derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t/2})={e}^{t/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}2{e}^{t/2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{t/2})}^{2}+{({e}^{t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}2{e}^{t/2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}2{e}^{t/2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}(1+{e}^{t})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{t/2}\\cdot {e}^{t/2}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the last integral using the substitution $u=1+{e}^{t}.$ Then, $\\text{d}u={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ We also need to compute new limits, given below.\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{4}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\pi \\cdot {\\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}({4}^{3/2}-{2}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}(8-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\pi }{3}(4-\\sqrt{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554653 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554653 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1aa63779-111f-54e9-892c-0fb614322783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554653 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186554602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554680 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554680 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "67d2476e-8b28-5c63-84c6-efc8f7cef93c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554680 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186367463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554693 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554693 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83dd259c-644a-5187-abca-3fbeaba6c996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554693 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186269200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554697 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554697 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "86a8d041-feed-5f21-a7aa-0238cf6d1240" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554697 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186530454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554707 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9479a2f7-46a4-5db5-a1e5-a589077eded2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554707 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186530493 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
